<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26730" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lintĕum</span></b> , i, n.
		linum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a linen cloth</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linteum cape atque exterge tibi manus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 1, 3, 110</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uncto linteo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Bacch. 3, 3, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linteum extersui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Curc. 4, 4, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">merces linteis et vitro delatae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rab. Post. 14, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">succinctus linteo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sucus linteo colatus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					25, 13, 103, § 164</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sella, linteisque lorisque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					2, 57, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lintea componit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					3, 263</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Linen</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tarquinienses (polliciti sunt) lintea in vela,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					28, 45</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A sail</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">certum est dare lintea retro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 686</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non tibi sunt integra lintea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 14, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zephyri veniant in lintea pleni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 2, 11, 41</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A girdle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut qui quaerere velit, nudus quaerat, linteo
					cinctus, lancem habens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gai. Inst. 3, § 192</span></i>
			; cf. also licium.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<i>A curtain</i>, used as a sign: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inscripta lintea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 168</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<i>Stuff, cloth</i>, other than linen, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				10, 21, § 38 sq.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
